# {{CLIENT}} source pack — `{{BUCKET}}/_md/`

Derived markdown conversion of the raw materials in this bucket ({{BUCKET_LABEL}}). Originals
live one level up in their own folders and are **never edited**; everything here is generated.

**Scope of this bucket:** {{BUCKET_SCOPE}} Boundary + flow rules: `../../README.md`.

**Read order:** this README → `00_REFERENCE_SUMMARY.md` (facts) → `01_REFERENCE_INSIGHTS.md`
(interpretation) → the per-topic source MD (only when you need to quote).

## Conversion conventions
- **One MD per source file**, in the matching `NN_<topic>/` folder, with `## Page N:` / `## Slide N:` /
  `## Section N:` anchors so any claim downstream can cite `<file>.md §Page 12`.
- **Header on each MD:** source path, page/slide count, date shared, author/origin if known,
  CONFIDENTIAL marker if applicable.
- **Tables** rendered as markdown tables; captions written from surrounding text.

## Image / OCR rule (lossless)
Every image is triaged into one bucket, by `scripts/triage_images.py` — never by hand:
decorative → deleted with a recorded reason (logos, borders, backgrounds); content → kept, placed
where it sat in the source, under a caption that says what it shows so a reader of this markdown
never has to open it; and where the figure's words did not survive text extraction, those words
are captured inline in a collapsible block. A figure whose text is not yet captured is never
deleted.

(Deliberately prose, not a tagged list: the triage tags are what the lint counts, so a README
that spells them out would report itself as untriaged work forever.)

